prompt:
Implement one bounded revenue-support improvement in the buyer scout promotion plan.

ONLY MODIFY:
- empire_os/buyer_scout_promotion_plan.py
- tests/test_buyer_scout_promotion_plan.py

GOAL:
Carry a single verified first-party email into the proposed canonical prospect payload so reviewed buyer candidates can move from research to contact resolution without manual stitching.

REQUIREMENTS:
1. In build_promotion_plan(), when site_evidence.first_party_emails contains exactly one nonblank email, set proposed_prospect_payload["contact_email"] to that email.
2. When there are zero emails or more than one email, contact_email must be None. Unknown stays unknown; do not guess or pick among ambiguous emails.
3. Preserve first_party_emails_preserved_for_identity_resolution exactly as evidence.
4. Add tests proving:
   - exactly one email becomes contact_email;
   - multiple emails fail closed to contact_email=None;
   - no email gives contact_email=None.
5. Preserve all existing behavior:
   - OBSERVE mode;
   - buy_signal_score remains None;
   - outreach_authorized remains False;
   - no database writes;
   - no canonical promotion;
   - no buyer creation;
   - no fabricated identity data.
6. Do not touch outbound send logic, payments, database migrations, environment, systemd, recovery/, toop/, or unrelated files.

VERIFY:
PYTHONPATH=/srv/empire_os /srv/empire_os/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_buyer_scout_promotion_plan.py --tb=short

Keep the patch minimal and production-quality.
